WEBVTT

00:00:07.007 --> 00:00:09.635
Commander!

00:00:09.676 --> 00:00:11.143
Look at this.

00:00:11.177 --> 00:00:12.644
I think they're
some kind of apple.

00:00:12.679 --> 00:00:13.646
Hmm.

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:14.977
There are trees filled with them

00:00:15.048 --> 00:00:17.312
as far as the eye can see,
just over that ridge.

00:00:17.350 --> 00:00:18.977
Kaylos. Ah.

00:00:19.019 --> 00:00:22.318
Aren't they gorgeous?

00:00:22.355 --> 00:00:23.788
One bite'll kill you.

00:00:23.823 --> 00:00:26.087
Puff you up like a vakol fish.

00:00:26.126 --> 00:00:30.153
Yeah, first your windpipe
swells...

00:00:30.196 --> 00:00:31.322
and just when you think

00:00:31.364 --> 00:00:33.491
you're going to die
of suffocation...

00:00:33.533 --> 00:00:36.434
Ow! Oh, you get a sharp pain
in your knees,

00:00:36.469 --> 00:00:40.200
which begins to work
its way right up to...

00:00:40.240 --> 00:00:42.538
I think we get the picture.

00:00:42.575 --> 00:00:44.008
Sorry, Mr. Carey.

00:00:44.077 --> 00:00:47.444
Just remember
the old trader's axiom:

00:00:47.480 --> 00:00:50.381
Never judge a fruit by its skin.

00:00:50.417 --> 00:00:53.181
On the other hand,
huh, take a bite.

00:00:53.219 --> 00:00:54.686
What is it?

00:00:54.721 --> 00:00:56.552
A leola root.

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:03.053
You expect us to eat this?

00:01:03.096 --> 00:01:06.190
This is the reason
I brought you here, Commander.

00:01:06.232 --> 00:01:07.631
There's no better source

00:01:07.667 --> 00:01:09.294
of vitamins and minerals
in the Quadrant

00:01:09.335 --> 00:01:10.962
than in this,
this ugly little root.

00:01:11.037 --> 00:01:14.370
I'd find the second-best source
acceptable if it tasted better.

00:01:15.508 --> 00:01:16.702
You humans!

00:01:16.743 --> 00:01:19.439
You're not used to roughing it,
are you?

00:01:19.479 --> 00:01:21.606
Well, take it
from one who knows.

00:01:21.648 --> 00:01:24.082
The day may come
when you'll relish

00:01:24.117 --> 00:01:25.982
every last crunch of leola.

00:01:28.188 --> 00:01:30.850
Stewed for a few hours
in a light herbal broth,

00:01:30.890 --> 00:01:32.881
ah, you won't even notice
the mildew.

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:44.663
Captain, I don't
think we're alone.

00:01:44.704 --> 00:01:47.298
Mr. Tuvok, run a lateral
EM scan for me,

00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:50.776
coordinates 81 mark 40.

00:01:50.810 --> 00:01:53.005
Running scan.

00:01:53.046 --> 00:01:54.240
What do you see, Mr. Paris?

00:01:54.280 --> 00:01:56.680
It's like a reflection.

00:01:56.716 --> 00:01:57.876
Something in low orbit.

00:01:57.917 --> 00:01:59.817
When it moves into
a certain angle from the sun...

00:01:59.853 --> 00:02:00.911
He's correct.

00:02:00.954 --> 00:02:03.115
I am picking up
an ionization trail.

00:02:03.156 --> 00:02:05.124
There is another ship in orbit.

00:02:05.158 --> 00:02:06.955
Using some kind
of cloaking device?

00:02:06.993 --> 00:02:10.121
It's not a cloaking device
as we know it, Captain.

00:02:10.163 --> 00:02:11.596
I cannot say for certain
what it is,

00:02:11.631 --> 00:02:13.826
but the ship does employ
some kind of masking circuitry

00:02:13.867 --> 00:02:15.095
that has affected our sensors.

00:02:15.135 --> 00:02:16.397
Voyager to away team.

00:02:16.436 --> 00:02:17.960
Go ahead, Captain.

00:02:18.071 --> 00:02:21.006
Any unexpected life signs
down there, Commander?

00:02:23.476 --> 00:02:25.171
Nothing but bloodworms.

00:02:25.211 --> 00:02:27.679
Neelix wants to bring
some back for a tartar

00:02:27.714 --> 00:02:29.181
he wants to make.

00:02:29.215 --> 00:02:30.443
I'm trying
to talk him out of it.

00:02:30.483 --> 00:02:32.576
We're picking up an unidentified
ship in low orbit.

00:02:32.619 --> 00:02:34.644
Collect your teams,
and prepare to transport back

00:02:34.687 --> 00:02:35.847
while we investigate.

00:02:35.889 --> 00:02:36.856
Acknowledged.

00:02:36.890 --> 00:02:38.619
Chakotay out.

00:02:38.658 --> 00:02:42.719
All units, report
to transport site A immediately.

00:02:42.762 --> 00:02:44.753
Captain, I believe
a polaron burst

00:02:44.797 --> 00:02:46.424
may give us visual contact.

00:02:46.466 --> 00:02:48.229
Do it.

00:02:54.040 --> 00:02:55.803
Kazon.

00:02:55.842 --> 00:02:58.003
The hull design does conform
to known specifications

00:02:58.044 --> 00:02:59.136
of the Kazon-Nistrim sect.

00:02:59.179 --> 00:03:00.476
Voyager to away teams.

00:03:00.513 --> 00:03:01.605
Return to the ship immediately.

00:03:01.648 --> 00:03:03.946
Acknowledged, Captain.

00:03:04.017 --> 00:03:07.180
Transporter Room, get ready
to begin on my command.

00:03:07.220 --> 00:03:08.619
Where is Ensign Seska?

00:03:10.623 --> 00:03:12.318
Chakotay to Seska.

00:03:13.560 --> 00:03:16.757
Transporter Room, can you locate
Ensign Seska's combadge signal?

00:03:16.796 --> 00:03:17.956
Negative, Commander.

00:03:18.031 --> 00:03:20.192
I'm not reading any sign of her.

00:03:20.233 --> 00:03:22.599
She was picking berries
with our group,

00:03:22.635 --> 00:03:24.102
over by the hillside.

00:03:24.137 --> 00:03:25.729
There were caves nearby.

00:03:25.772 --> 00:03:26.830
If she went inside one,

00:03:26.873 --> 00:03:28.738
it might be blocking
her combadge signal.

00:03:28.775 --> 00:03:30.504
The rest of you get
back to the ship.

00:03:30.543 --> 00:03:31.874
I'm going to look for her.

00:04:44.517 --> 00:04:45.779
Oh, thank the Prophets!

00:04:45.818 --> 00:04:47.149
What are you doing here?

00:04:47.186 --> 00:04:49.916
Mushrooms. I saw them growing
by the mouth of the cave.

00:04:49.956 --> 00:04:52.982
I wanted to teach Neelix
how to make your favorite soup.

00:04:53.092 --> 00:04:56.357
I appreciate the thought, but
we've got to get out of here.

00:07:00.651 --> 00:07:04.644
Captain's Log, Stardate 48658.2.

00:07:04.689 --> 00:07:06.350
We successfully left orbit

00:07:06.391 --> 00:07:08.916
without further interference
from the Kazon.

00:07:08.993 --> 00:07:11.223
Commander Chakotay was injured

00:07:11.262 --> 00:07:13.856
but is recovering
from his wounds.

00:07:17.468 --> 00:07:19.436
Come in.

00:07:23.775 --> 00:07:25.936
I didn't think I'd make it.

00:07:25.977 --> 00:07:27.274
Feeling better?

00:07:27.311 --> 00:07:29.905
Yeah.
What have you got there?

00:07:32.850 --> 00:07:34.477
Real food.

00:07:34.519 --> 00:07:36.817
You got Neelix to make
some mushroom soup.

00:07:36.854 --> 00:07:37.912
Are you kidding?

00:07:37.955 --> 00:07:40.185
The man wanted
to stretch the mushrooms

00:07:40.224 --> 00:07:41.452
with just a little...

00:07:41.492 --> 00:07:42.823
- leola root.
- Leola root.

00:07:42.860 --> 00:07:44.259
We got into this tug of war

00:07:44.295 --> 00:07:46.388
with the bag of mushrooms
in the middle.

00:07:46.431 --> 00:07:48.899
It was the most ludicrous
thing you've ever seen.

00:07:48.933 --> 00:07:50.400
Tuvok and Kes broke us up,

00:07:50.435 --> 00:07:52.801
and then Neelix
threw me out of his kitchen.

00:07:52.837 --> 00:07:53.895
So, how did you?

00:07:53.938 --> 00:07:55.269
Mm, strictly a Maquis operation.

00:07:55.306 --> 00:07:56.398
Hmm!

00:07:56.441 --> 00:07:59.968
First, we arranged
for a little morale crisis.

00:08:00.011 --> 00:08:01.376
A couple of our people

00:08:01.412 --> 00:08:04.245
suddenly came down
with severe homesickness.

00:08:04.282 --> 00:08:06.409
Neelix, our devoted
morale officer,

00:08:06.451 --> 00:08:10.046
responded to the call
and came in to cheer them up,

00:08:10.088 --> 00:08:12.784
and while they were
all singing Rakan folk songs,

00:08:12.824 --> 00:08:15.122
Jackson and I
broke into the kitchen.

00:08:17.862 --> 00:08:20.092
You looted the food reserves?

00:08:20.131 --> 00:08:24.329
Well, if he's not going
to give us a decent meal...

00:08:26.637 --> 00:08:28.468
I can't believe you did this.

00:08:28.506 --> 00:08:31.634
Well, it's not like
we're hiding anything.

00:08:31.676 --> 00:08:35.134
I did bring soup straight
to the First Officer, didn't I?

00:08:35.179 --> 00:08:38.376
Thanks for including me
in a criminal conspiracy.

00:08:38.416 --> 00:08:40.281
Does he know about this yet?

00:08:40.318 --> 00:08:44.482
Well, the morale crisis ended
a few minutes ago, so I'd say...

00:08:44.522 --> 00:08:46.046
Neelix to Chakotay.

00:08:46.090 --> 00:08:48.456
...that he probably does.

00:08:48.493 --> 00:08:49.960
Go ahead, Neelix.

00:08:49.994 --> 00:08:51.621
I'd like to report a crime.

00:08:51.662 --> 00:08:53.459
Someone has broken into
my kitchen and stolen food...

00:08:53.498 --> 00:08:56.490
taken food out of the mouths
of their crewmates.

00:08:56.534 --> 00:08:57.501
I know.

00:08:57.535 --> 00:08:59.196
It was that Seska, wasn't it?

00:08:59.237 --> 00:09:02.263
I promise you everyone involved
will be disciplined.

00:09:02.306 --> 00:09:05.036
If you'd like my recommendations
for punishment...

00:09:05.076 --> 00:09:06.771
Thank you.
I'll handle that.

00:09:06.811 --> 00:09:08.472
Chakotay out.

00:09:10.214 --> 00:09:13.149
Replicator privileges
revoked for two days.

00:09:13.184 --> 00:09:14.742
Everyone, including me.

00:09:14.785 --> 00:09:16.548
They're not going to do it.

00:09:16.587 --> 00:09:19.454
Then I'll personally
put them in the brig.

00:09:19.490 --> 00:09:21.958
You'd put me in the brig?

00:09:23.294 --> 00:09:25.728
After all we've been through?

00:09:32.570 --> 00:09:35.266
The soup was worth losing
the replicator privileges

00:09:35.306 --> 00:09:38.366
for two days... admit it.

00:09:38.409 --> 00:09:39.933
That's not the point.

00:09:40.011 --> 00:09:42.343
I get the point.

00:09:42.380 --> 00:09:44.109
Can we make up now?

00:09:49.687 --> 00:09:52.918
Who else knows how to make
your favorite soup like I do?

00:09:52.957 --> 00:09:54.948
No one...

00:09:54.992 --> 00:09:58.086
but we agreed a long time ago,
this wouldn't work.

00:10:02.967 --> 00:10:04.628
Look around, Chakotay.

00:10:04.669 --> 00:10:08.036
There aren't that many
potential mates out here.

00:10:12.944 --> 00:10:16.402
Of course, if you're
not interested...

00:10:16.447 --> 00:10:19.905
I have had my eye
on young Ensign Kim.

00:10:25.623 --> 00:10:27.454
Janeway to all senior officers.

00:10:27.491 --> 00:10:29.686
Please report to the Bridge.

00:10:31.362 --> 00:10:36.163
We require help... immediately!

00:10:36.200 --> 00:10:40.102
Anyone who can hear
this message, please help!

00:10:40.137 --> 00:10:41.536
Long-range scanners

00:10:41.572 --> 00:10:43.199
picked up the distress signal
three minutes ago.

00:10:43.241 --> 00:10:45.573
The ship's
dimensions are identical

00:10:45.610 --> 00:10:47.237
to the vessel
we encountered at the planet.

00:10:47.278 --> 00:10:48.677
It is a Kazon-Nistrim
ship, Captain.

00:10:48.713 --> 00:10:51.409
Captain, this may be a trap.

00:10:51.449 --> 00:10:55.249
The Kazon-Nistrim is one
of the most violent sects

00:10:55.286 --> 00:10:56.947
in the entire Kazon Collective.

00:10:56.988 --> 00:10:59.286
We need immediate assistance!

00:10:59.323 --> 00:11:03.555
We have lost
all Bridge operations.

00:11:03.594 --> 00:11:06.529
Barely able to function.

00:11:06.564 --> 00:11:09.965
Please... assist!

00:11:10.067 --> 00:11:12.797
Mr. Kim, can you determine

00:11:12.837 --> 00:11:15.806
if this ship
has sustained genuine damage?

00:11:15.840 --> 00:11:18.308
There are fluctuating
nucleonic patterns.

00:11:18.342 --> 00:11:21.311
It might indicate
a reactor breakdown on board.

00:11:21.345 --> 00:11:24.678
Mr. Paris, run an extended
scanner sequence

00:11:24.715 --> 00:11:26.649
to identify
any other Kazon ships

00:11:26.684 --> 00:11:28.015
that might be in the area.

00:11:29.253 --> 00:11:30.982
Nothing showing up, Captain.

00:11:31.088 --> 00:11:33.750
Maintain scans
and set a heading to intercept.

00:11:33.791 --> 00:11:35.258
New heading entered.

00:11:35.293 --> 00:11:37.454
I take your warning seriously,
Neelix,

00:11:37.495 --> 00:11:41.454
and will act with caution,
but if we can help, we should.

00:11:41.499 --> 00:11:43.990
Besides,
this may be an opportunity

00:11:44.035 --> 00:11:47.766
to make a friend,
and out here,

00:11:47.805 --> 00:11:51.172
we can use all the friends
we can get.

00:12:45.796 --> 00:12:48.264
What could do
something like this?

00:12:48.299 --> 00:12:51.234
I'm showing high levels
of nucleonic radiation.

00:12:51.268 --> 00:12:54.829
It seems to be isolated
in that area.

00:12:54.872 --> 00:12:55.998
It is likely that the ship's

00:12:56.107 --> 00:12:58.007
automatic containment
systems were activated

00:12:58.075 --> 00:13:00.873
when the radiation
entered the Bridge.

00:13:00.911 --> 00:13:03.106
We should be safe
as long as we stay

00:13:03.147 --> 00:13:04.876
on this side of the force field.

00:13:10.621 --> 00:13:13.317
Someone's alive over here.

00:13:23.667 --> 00:13:25.532
Away team to Voyager.

00:13:25.569 --> 00:13:28.197
We've got a single male Kazon
alive on the Bridge.

00:13:28.239 --> 00:13:30.070
Transport him
directly to Sick Bay.

00:13:30.107 --> 00:13:32.007
Energizing.

00:13:34.278 --> 00:13:36.906
It appears the explosion
emanated from this console.

00:13:36.947 --> 00:13:39.279
Something look a little odd
about it to you?

00:13:39.316 --> 00:13:41.375
The structural pattern
does not conform

00:13:41.419 --> 00:13:42.784
to the rest of the Bridge.

00:13:42.820 --> 00:13:45.084
No, there's something
else strange about it.

00:13:45.122 --> 00:13:48.990
The residue has a.41 percent
trace of a neosorium composite,

00:13:49.059 --> 00:13:52.256
and I don't know anyone
who uses neosorium technology,

00:13:52.296 --> 00:13:54.491
except for the Federation.

00:13:54.532 --> 00:13:58.468
So how did it get
into the hands of the Kazon?

00:14:02.506 --> 00:14:04.235
Incredible.

00:14:04.275 --> 00:14:08.109
Somehow, virtually every cell
in his body has been altered.

00:14:08.145 --> 00:14:09.612
Altered?

00:14:09.647 --> 00:14:11.205
His cells have mutated,

00:14:11.248 --> 00:14:14.081
or they've been fused
with inorganic matter.

00:14:14.118 --> 00:14:15.346
I can't make heads
or tails of it.

00:14:15.386 --> 00:14:16.478
Look at this.

00:14:16.520 --> 00:14:19.080
His blood cells have bonded
with metallic nuclei.

00:14:19.123 --> 00:14:21.318
The crew members
closest to the explosion

00:14:21.358 --> 00:14:22.518
were virtually melded

00:14:22.560 --> 00:14:24.494
with huge pieces
of metal fragments.

00:14:24.528 --> 00:14:26.189
He was luckier than the others.

00:14:26.230 --> 00:14:28.460
That remains to be seen.

00:14:28.499 --> 00:14:30.626
I'm going to have to do
a complete pyrocyte replacement

00:14:30.668 --> 00:14:31.965
if we're going
to keep him alive.

00:14:32.002 --> 00:14:35.267
We'd better hope there are
compatible donors on board.

00:14:35.306 --> 00:14:37.638
I'll run a cytological
screening of the crew.

00:14:37.675 --> 00:14:40.906
We'll let you know the results
as soon as we can.

00:14:43.714 --> 00:14:46.774
Captain, there was an apparent
Federation signature

00:14:46.817 --> 00:14:47.841
to the explosion.

00:14:47.885 --> 00:14:49.113
What?

00:14:49.153 --> 00:14:51.121
It looked like
they were trying to install

00:14:51.155 --> 00:14:52.816
some new technology
that detonated.

00:14:52.857 --> 00:14:54.415
You're saying
they have some kind

00:14:54.458 --> 00:14:55.891
of Federation weapon on board?

00:14:55.926 --> 00:14:58.554
A console on the Bridge
was the source of the explosion.

00:14:58.596 --> 00:15:00.257
We're not sure
what its function was,

00:15:00.297 --> 00:15:01.924
and it's going
to be hard to get to.

00:15:02.032 --> 00:15:03.431
We can't transport it out?

00:15:03.467 --> 00:15:07.301
Not with those levels
of nucleonic radiation.

00:15:07.338 --> 00:15:08.703
The transporter beam
would disperse

00:15:08.739 --> 00:15:10.297
the moment it hit
the irradiated cabin.

00:15:10.341 --> 00:15:12.536
How could they possibly
have Federation technology?

00:15:12.576 --> 00:15:13.941
There are only
three alternatives

00:15:14.044 --> 00:15:15.534
I can discern at this time.

00:15:15.579 --> 00:15:17.945
One: It is not
Federation technology at all

00:15:18.015 --> 00:15:20.313
but something similar.

00:15:20.351 --> 00:15:21.511
Bridge.

00:15:21.552 --> 00:15:23.782
Two:
Another Federation starship

00:15:23.821 --> 00:15:25.846
may have been brought
to the Delta Quadrant

00:15:25.890 --> 00:15:26.948
prior to our arrival,

00:15:27.024 --> 00:15:29.219
and they interacted
with the Kazon-Nistrim.

00:15:29.260 --> 00:15:30.955
Were there any other reports
of missing starships?

00:15:31.028 --> 00:15:32.620
Not to my knowledge.

00:15:32.663 --> 00:15:34.858
Three: Someone from this ship

00:15:34.899 --> 00:15:36.958
has covertly given technology
to the Kazon.

00:15:37.001 --> 00:15:39.629
Computer, hold turbolift.

00:15:42.006 --> 00:15:44.668
I don't like
number three at all, Tuvok.

00:15:44.708 --> 00:15:47.802
Nevertheless, it is the most
probable explanation.

00:15:47.845 --> 00:15:49.278
It may not be a coincidence

00:15:49.313 --> 00:15:51.975
that the Kazon ship
we encountered at the planet

00:15:52.016 --> 00:15:53.745
was able to deceive our sensors.

00:15:53.784 --> 00:15:56.082
Perhaps someone transmitted
instructions to them

00:15:56.120 --> 00:15:57.417
before we arrived.

00:15:59.657 --> 00:16:00.851
I want you to personally

00:16:00.891 --> 00:16:02.882
go through
the transmission logs, Tuvok.

00:16:02.927 --> 00:16:04.758
Compare them
to the actual telemetry.

00:16:04.795 --> 00:16:08.561
See if there's any evidence
of prior contact with the Kazon.

00:16:08.599 --> 00:16:10.533
Who would have had a chance
to meet with them

00:16:10.568 --> 00:16:11.865
while you were on the surface?

00:16:11.902 --> 00:16:12.926
A dozen people.

00:16:12.970 --> 00:16:14.562
We were scattered
all over the area.

00:16:14.605 --> 00:16:17.369
You did discover Ensign Seska
in proximity to them.

00:16:17.408 --> 00:16:20.707
Seska almost killed me
because she thought I was Kazon.

00:16:20.744 --> 00:16:22.939
She wouldn't
do something like this.

00:16:22.980 --> 00:16:25.949
Nevertheless, I urge you
to regard her with caution

00:16:26.016 --> 00:16:27.142
for the time being.

00:16:29.486 --> 00:16:32.944
Why would anyone
on this ship betray us?

00:16:32.990 --> 00:16:35.788
We're all in this together.

00:16:35.826 --> 00:16:38.488
We need to retrieve that console
and get some answers

00:16:38.529 --> 00:16:40.554
before the rumors
get out of hand.

00:16:40.598 --> 00:16:42.589
Computer, resume.

00:16:47.671 --> 00:16:49.696
Releasing the force field
isn't an option.

00:16:49.740 --> 00:16:52.573
That would just allow the
radiation into the whole cabin.

00:16:52.610 --> 00:16:54.805
We could generate
a localized subspace bubble

00:16:54.845 --> 00:16:56.210
to get past the force field.

00:16:56.246 --> 00:16:58.680
One minor subspace disruption
and you're dead.

00:16:58.716 --> 00:17:00.149
It's too risky.

00:17:00.184 --> 00:17:01.451
I'd be willing to risk it.

00:17:01.584 --> 00:17:05.213
We could use an expander

00:17:05.254 --> 00:17:07.347
to manipulate
the containment field.

00:17:08.524 --> 00:17:09.616
Manipulate it how?

00:17:11.027 --> 00:17:12.619
Move it out of the way.

00:17:12.662 --> 00:17:15.756
Rotate the field, and the
radiation trapped inside it

00:17:15.798 --> 00:17:16.924
away from the console.

00:17:16.999 --> 00:17:19.297
Once it's clear, we have access.

00:17:19.335 --> 00:17:21.803
How long will it
take to set this up?

00:17:21.838 --> 00:17:25.137
We, uh, we should be able
to make an attempt by tomorrow.

00:17:25.174 --> 00:17:26.801
I want it ready
by the end of the day.

00:17:26.843 --> 00:17:28.037
No, Captain.

00:17:28.077 --> 00:17:30.671
When I say tomorrow,
I mean tomorrow.

00:17:30.713 --> 00:17:31.941
I don't exaggerate.

00:17:32.048 --> 00:17:34.346
Tomorrow is the best I can do.

00:17:34.383 --> 00:17:36.010
Understood, Lieutenant.

00:17:38.020 --> 00:17:39.419
All right...

00:17:39.455 --> 00:17:41.946
we'll begin on the Kazon Bridge.

00:17:41.991 --> 00:17:43.891
Carey, Nicoletti, Seska.

00:17:43.926 --> 00:17:45.826
No. I want Ensign Seska

00:17:45.862 --> 00:17:49.491
to coordinate the operation
from our Bridge.

00:17:49.532 --> 00:17:51.864
Okay, Henard, you're with us.

00:17:51.901 --> 00:17:53.027
Dismissed.

00:17:56.105 --> 00:17:57.299
What was that all about?

00:17:57.340 --> 00:17:58.307
What?

00:17:58.341 --> 00:17:59.638
Oh, you know
what I'm talking about.

00:17:59.675 --> 00:18:01.370
There's nothing important
to do on the Bridge.

00:18:01.410 --> 00:18:02.877
I disagree.
We need someone up there...

00:18:02.912 --> 00:18:04.675
What the hell is going on?

00:18:08.718 --> 00:18:10.208
There's some concern about you.

00:18:12.488 --> 00:18:15.116
What kind of concern?

00:18:15.157 --> 00:18:18.422
Concern because I found you
near the Kazon on the planet.

00:18:18.461 --> 00:18:19.928
Oh, I see.

00:18:19.962 --> 00:18:21.452
So now I'm a traitor.

00:18:21.497 --> 00:18:23.362
I sell technology to the enemy?

00:18:23.399 --> 00:18:24.696
- I don't believe that.
- No, you just take me

00:18:24.734 --> 00:18:26.258
off my assignment.

00:18:26.302 --> 00:18:28.793
I'm trying to take you out
of harm's way to protect you.

00:18:28.838 --> 00:18:29.930
This is your idea of protection?

00:18:30.006 --> 00:18:31.371
You might as well
point a finger at me

00:18:31.407 --> 00:18:32.567
in front of the entire crew.

00:18:32.608 --> 00:18:34.769
You don't assign someone
you don't trust to the Bridge.

00:18:37.046 --> 00:18:38.513
Look, I'm sorry,

00:18:38.548 --> 00:18:40.812
but if something goes wrong
over there, I don't want you

00:18:40.850 --> 00:18:42.442
anywhere near it.

00:18:42.485 --> 00:18:44.680
Thanks for your concern.

00:18:55.431 --> 00:18:56.728
How is he?

00:18:56.766 --> 00:18:58.427
Not very good.

00:18:58.467 --> 00:19:01.732
We need to completely
replace his blood.

00:19:12.415 --> 00:19:15.509
Will he regain consciousness?

00:19:15.551 --> 00:19:16.916
I'm not sure.

00:19:16.953 --> 00:19:18.921
Even if he does,
there's no way to predict

00:19:18.955 --> 00:19:22.789
what kind of brain damage
there might be.

00:19:22.825 --> 00:19:24.315
He's the only one
who really knows

00:19:24.360 --> 00:19:26.555
what happened on that ship,
Doctor.

00:19:26.596 --> 00:19:29.929
The only one who can tell them
I had nothing to do with it.

00:19:30.032 --> 00:19:31.522
You? I don't understand.

00:19:31.567 --> 00:19:33.831
Would you call me
right away if he wakes up?

00:19:33.869 --> 00:19:35.860
All right.

00:19:38.908 --> 00:19:41.775
Ensign...

00:19:41.811 --> 00:19:42.778
did you ever come in

00:19:42.812 --> 00:19:45.076
to leave a blood sample on file?

00:19:45.114 --> 00:19:48.675
No. I never got around to it.

00:19:48.718 --> 00:19:50.049
Why?

00:19:50.086 --> 00:19:52.816
I've been running a crew
compatibility analysis,

00:19:52.855 --> 00:19:54.220
and your file never came up.

00:19:54.256 --> 00:19:55.780
My blood won't help you.

00:19:55.825 --> 00:19:58.293
I had a childhood disease
that infected it.

00:19:58.327 --> 00:20:01.160
I was warned never to donate
blood for a transfusion.

00:20:01.197 --> 00:20:04.223
All the more reason we should
have your blood on file.

00:20:05.334 --> 00:20:06.494
I will.

00:20:06.535 --> 00:20:09.197
Right now, I have something
more important to take care of.

00:20:12.375 --> 00:20:14.434
Someone did make
an unauthorized transmission.

00:20:14.477 --> 00:20:16.968
And whoever it was was an expert
at covering their tracks.

00:20:17.079 --> 00:20:19.513
The signal was masked
by a test of the dorsal emitters

00:20:19.548 --> 00:20:20.879
that we conducted a week ago.

00:20:20.916 --> 00:20:22.213
Who was working on that test?

00:20:22.251 --> 00:20:23.479
Only the whole Engineering crew.

00:20:23.519 --> 00:20:24.884
We're trying
to trace the station

00:20:24.920 --> 00:20:26.080
where the signal originated.

00:20:26.122 --> 00:20:27.851
Again, the perpetrator
was skilled enough

00:20:27.890 --> 00:20:30.324
to make the tracking process
extremely difficult for us.

00:20:30.359 --> 00:20:32.953
It's like working backwards
through a maze of circuits.

00:20:32.995 --> 00:20:34.462
We keep bumping into dead ends.

00:20:34.497 --> 00:20:36.124
Paris to Captain Janeway.

00:20:36.165 --> 00:20:38.429
Please report to the Bridge.

00:20:41.671 --> 00:20:43.502
Captain, another Kazon ship
is approaching,

00:20:43.539 --> 00:20:44.938
trying to hail
the disabled ship.

00:20:44.974 --> 00:20:46.498
They're not
within visual range yet.

00:20:46.542 --> 00:20:48.601
Perhaps someone else
picked up the distress call.

00:20:48.644 --> 00:20:50.669
What's their ETA?

00:20:50.713 --> 00:20:52.943
At their current speed,
four hours, 20 minutes.

00:20:52.982 --> 00:20:54.449
Should I tell them we're here?

00:20:54.483 --> 00:20:55.848
If we know about them,

00:20:55.885 --> 00:20:58.649
it's a good bet
they know about us.

00:20:58.688 --> 00:21:01.953
We don't have anything good
to tell them.

00:21:01.991 --> 00:21:03.549
I think we'll wait.

00:21:03.592 --> 00:21:05.787
Captain, I'm showing
an unauthorized autosequence

00:21:05.828 --> 00:21:06.795
in Transporter Room 2.

00:21:06.829 --> 00:21:08.956
Someone's left Voyager.

00:21:08.998 --> 00:21:11.193
Computer, identify
who just beamed off the ship

00:21:11.233 --> 00:21:12.393
from Transporter Room 2.

00:21:12.435 --> 00:21:13.800
Ensign Seska.

00:21:28.551 --> 00:21:30.075
Chakotay to Seska.

00:21:30.119 --> 00:21:31.552
I really don't have time

00:21:31.587 --> 00:21:33.646
to talk to you right now,
Chakotay.

00:21:33.689 --> 00:21:34.986
What the hell
do you think you're doing?

00:21:35.091 --> 00:21:37.082
Retrieving the console, my way.

00:21:37.126 --> 00:21:39.356
I want you back on this ship,
and I mean now.

00:21:39.395 --> 00:21:41.522
The Captain said she wanted
the console today.

00:21:41.564 --> 00:21:43.623
Carey's plan
couldn't do it in time,

00:21:43.666 --> 00:21:44.963
but mine can.

00:21:45.000 --> 00:21:46.297
Captain, it is conceivable

00:21:46.335 --> 00:21:47.996
that she has gone
to the Kazon ship

00:21:48.104 --> 00:21:50.004
to destroy evidence
that might implicate her.

00:21:50.072 --> 00:21:52.097
She's gone back to the Kazon
ship to prove herself to us.

00:21:52.141 --> 00:21:53.267
Can't you see that?

00:21:53.309 --> 00:21:54.469
I've got a lock on her, Captain.

00:21:54.510 --> 00:21:55.875
Do you want me
to transport her back?

00:21:55.911 --> 00:21:57.344
If we try to beam her out

00:21:57.379 --> 00:21:59.313
while she's
manipulating subspace,

00:21:59.348 --> 00:22:00.508
we might kill her.

00:22:03.619 --> 00:22:05.917
Chakotay to Seska.

00:22:05.955 --> 00:22:09.118
Seska, respond.

00:22:09.158 --> 00:22:10.284
Get her out of there!

00:22:10.326 --> 00:22:11.884
Send her to Sick Bay.

00:22:11.927 --> 00:22:13.656
Energizing.

00:22:19.068 --> 00:22:20.797
Prep 3cc's kelotane.

00:22:20.836 --> 00:22:23.134
I'll need a dermal regenerator.

00:22:23.172 --> 00:22:25.163
Run a full blood scan.

00:22:42.525 --> 00:22:45.153
Have a seat, Mr. Carey.

00:22:53.035 --> 00:22:56.732
How have things been going
for you in Engineering?

00:22:56.772 --> 00:22:58.103
Fine.

00:22:58.140 --> 00:23:00.836
Why, is there a problem?

00:23:00.876 --> 00:23:03.811
You getting along all right
with Lieutenant Torres?

00:23:03.846 --> 00:23:06.610
I think we've settled
our differences.

00:23:06.649 --> 00:23:08.617
She was promoted
to Chief Engineer

00:23:08.651 --> 00:23:09.913
over you, Lieutenant.

00:23:09.952 --> 00:23:11.317
That might be difficult

00:23:11.353 --> 00:23:13.685
for someone in your position
to accept.

00:23:13.722 --> 00:23:17.283
Captain, I accepted
your decision,

00:23:17.326 --> 00:23:18.816
and I've worked as hard as I can

00:23:18.861 --> 00:23:22.058
to make myself a valuable member
of Lieutenant Torres' team.

00:23:22.097 --> 00:23:24.588
I can't believe
she'd have any complaints

00:23:24.633 --> 00:23:25.930
about my performance.

00:23:25.968 --> 00:23:27.367
She doesn't.

00:23:27.403 --> 00:23:30.736
Then what am I doing here?

00:23:32.174 --> 00:23:34.301
Lieutenant,
have you had any contact

00:23:34.343 --> 00:23:35.708
with the Kazon-Nistrim

00:23:35.744 --> 00:23:38.110
since we arrived
in the Delta Quadrant?

00:23:38.147 --> 00:23:40.945
What?!

00:23:40.983 --> 00:23:42.917
Y-You mean, me personally?

00:23:45.354 --> 00:23:47.788
No. Of course not.

00:23:47.823 --> 00:23:49.916
You were out of contact
for almost an hour

00:23:49.959 --> 00:23:52.257
on the planet
where we encountered the Kazon.

00:23:52.294 --> 00:23:55.991
You mean, when I was picking
those poison apples?

00:23:56.031 --> 00:23:57.794
What about before
we arrived at the planet?

00:23:57.833 --> 00:24:01.200
Did you have any reason
to signal a Kazon-Nistrim ship?

00:24:01.237 --> 00:24:02.932
- No.
- Nevertheless,

00:24:02.972 --> 00:24:05.668
a signal was sent to the Kazon
from your station in Engineering

00:24:05.708 --> 00:24:08.040
during our dorsal emitter test
last week.

00:24:08.077 --> 00:24:09.305
My station?

00:24:09.345 --> 00:24:11.472
Were you not in Engineering
at that time?

00:24:11.513 --> 00:24:15.108
Well, yes, I was, but...

00:24:15.150 --> 00:24:17.846
you know how it is down there
during a systems analysis.

00:24:17.887 --> 00:24:19.479
Did you see anyone else
at your station?

00:24:19.521 --> 00:24:21.455
Honestly, I don't remember.

00:24:21.490 --> 00:24:23.583
Maybe you should ask Seska.

00:24:23.626 --> 00:24:25.093
Why Seska?

00:24:25.127 --> 00:24:29.757
Everybody knows she was found
in the cave with the Kazon.

00:24:39.208 --> 00:24:43.372
Look, I'm not saying
she did anything wrong,

00:24:43.412 --> 00:24:45.471
but I didn't either.

00:24:45.514 --> 00:24:48.642
I'd like to believe you,
Mr. Carey,

00:24:48.684 --> 00:24:51.881
but somebody did contact
the Kazon,

00:24:51.921 --> 00:24:53.149
and until we know who,

00:24:53.188 --> 00:24:56.316
I'm going to have
to restrict you to quarters.

00:25:09.204 --> 00:25:10.728
What do you think?

00:25:11.974 --> 00:25:14.602
He had the motive
and the opportunity.

00:25:14.643 --> 00:25:17.635
He's also had a distinguished
Starfleet career.

00:25:17.680 --> 00:25:19.944
Seska spent most
of the last two years

00:25:19.982 --> 00:25:21.609
as an enemy of the Federation.

00:25:21.650 --> 00:25:22.878
So have I.

00:25:27.957 --> 00:25:30.255
Captain, we're being hailed
by the approaching Kazon ship.

00:25:30.292 --> 00:25:31.554
How soon will they be here?

00:25:31.593 --> 00:25:32.685
Four minutes.

00:25:32.728 --> 00:25:34.525
I wish we had something
more definitive to tell them.

00:25:34.563 --> 00:25:36.053
Open a channel.

00:25:38.434 --> 00:25:40.425
I am Kathryn Janeway,

00:25:40.469 --> 00:25:43.438
Captain of the Federation
Starship Voyager.

00:25:43.472 --> 00:25:47.909
My name is Culluh,
First Maje of the Kazon-Nistrim.

00:25:47.943 --> 00:25:51.106
What have you done to our ship?

00:25:52.448 --> 00:25:54.939
We responded to a call for help.

00:25:54.984 --> 00:25:57.145
Unfortunately, by the time
we were able to respond,

00:25:57.186 --> 00:25:59.814
all but one of the crew
were dead.

00:25:59.855 --> 00:26:02.756
I would like to speak
to the survivor.

00:26:02.791 --> 00:26:04.691
He hasn't
regained consciousness.

00:26:04.727 --> 00:26:05.921
We have him in our Sick Bay.

00:26:05.995 --> 00:26:08.429
We'd be happy to beam you aboard
so you can see him.

00:26:08.464 --> 00:26:11.194
You will prepare for my arrival.

00:26:12.901 --> 00:26:14.630
Friendly sort.

00:26:24.747 --> 00:26:26.874
Ah, Captain,
I'm glad you're here.

00:26:26.915 --> 00:26:29.179
I was just about to call you.

00:26:29.218 --> 00:26:32.210
Doctor, this is
First Maje Culluh,

00:26:32.254 --> 00:26:33.278
of the Kazon-Nistrim.

00:26:33.322 --> 00:26:35.586
Could you give us
the latest condition report

00:26:35.624 --> 00:26:36.955
on your Kazon patient?

00:26:36.992 --> 00:26:38.084
Well, the good news is,

00:26:38.127 --> 00:26:39.321
we've been able
to stabilize him.

00:26:39.361 --> 00:26:42.728
We had to completely
replace his blood.

00:26:42.765 --> 00:26:44.562
Replace his blood?

00:26:44.600 --> 00:26:46.329
With what?

00:26:46.368 --> 00:26:48.734
The blood of volunteers
from our crew.

00:26:48.771 --> 00:26:50.398
They saved his life.

00:26:50.439 --> 00:26:52.532
His own blood cells
were killing him.

00:26:52.574 --> 00:26:55.805
They were changed
by the accident on his ship.

00:26:55.844 --> 00:26:57.505
Changed in what manner?

00:26:57.546 --> 00:27:00.777
We haven't been able
to determine that yet.

00:27:00.816 --> 00:27:02.113
We've been working on a plan

00:27:02.151 --> 00:27:04.278
to access the source
of the explosion,

00:27:04.319 --> 00:27:06.887
which should answer
a lot of the questions.

00:27:07.020 --> 00:27:08.749
That will no longer
be necessary.

00:27:08.788 --> 00:27:12.280
We will take the damaged vessel
to our port for inspection.

00:27:12.325 --> 00:27:16.455
I'm afraid I can't allow you
to do that just yet.

00:27:16.496 --> 00:27:20.432
And what gives you the right
to interfere in our affairs?

00:27:20.467 --> 00:27:23.231
There was a trace
of a Federation compound

00:27:23.270 --> 00:27:25.397
in the remains of the explosion.

00:27:25.438 --> 00:27:27.030
We have reason to believe

00:27:27.073 --> 00:27:30.167
that someone on board
this ship gave technology

00:27:30.210 --> 00:27:31.370
to your people.

00:27:31.411 --> 00:27:34.938
Until we have a better
explanation of what occurred,

00:27:34.981 --> 00:27:37.040
I can't release
that ship to you.

00:27:37.083 --> 00:27:38.744
That is not acceptable.

00:27:38.785 --> 00:27:40.650
It will have to be.

00:27:40.687 --> 00:27:44.953
Your unique technologies
make you brave, Captain,

00:27:44.991 --> 00:27:47.357
but you have only one ship.

00:27:47.394 --> 00:27:48.952
In less than a day,

00:27:49.029 --> 00:27:51.964
there will be four Kazon vessels
off your bow.

00:27:51.998 --> 00:27:55.058
Perhaps by then,
we'll have the answers we need.

00:27:55.101 --> 00:27:57.569
You will leave us with him.

00:28:06.813 --> 00:28:09.043
I assume they'll want
to take him back to their ship.

00:28:09.082 --> 00:28:10.709
I'd rather not let them
do it just yet...

00:28:10.750 --> 00:28:12.115
in case he regains
consciousness.

00:28:12.152 --> 00:28:13.915
There are a lot of questions
he can answer.

00:28:13.987 --> 00:28:15.750
Can I tell them
it's not safe to move him?

00:28:15.789 --> 00:28:17.154
It would be the truth.

00:28:17.190 --> 00:28:18.179
Good.

00:28:32.138 --> 00:28:33.571
He's dead.

00:28:33.606 --> 00:28:35.870
Get off this ship.

00:28:39.713 --> 00:28:42.682
There was some kind of nerve
toxin in that needle.

00:28:42.716 --> 00:28:44.047
He died instantly.

00:28:48.288 --> 00:28:52.054
Captain, may we talk to you
in my office?

00:28:58.365 --> 00:28:59.923
It's about Seska.

00:28:59.966 --> 00:29:01.866
Complications?

00:29:01.901 --> 00:29:06.235
I was analyzing her blood
chemistry to try to locate

00:29:06.272 --> 00:29:08.399
a compatible donor.

00:29:08.441 --> 00:29:11.171
But when I got the results,
her blood was lacking

00:29:11.211 --> 00:29:13.338
all the common
Bajoran blood factors.

00:29:13.380 --> 00:29:14.608
Meaning?

00:29:14.647 --> 00:29:15.909
The only conclusion we can reach

00:29:15.982 --> 00:29:17.847
is that she is not,
in fact, Bajoran.

00:29:17.884 --> 00:29:21.320
It appears Seska has been
genetically altered.

00:29:21.354 --> 00:29:25.290
My suspicion is
she was born Cardassian.

00:29:35.769 --> 00:29:36.929
You're asking me to believe

00:29:37.037 --> 00:29:39.437
she's a Cardassian agent
who infiltrated the Maquis?

00:29:39.472 --> 00:29:41.736
Starfleet Security has
documented several incidents

00:29:41.775 --> 00:29:44.243
in which Cardassians
have used cosmetic alterations

00:29:44.277 --> 00:29:46.074
for the purpose
of infiltrating an enemy.

00:29:46.112 --> 00:29:48.273
This is crazy.
This is just impossible.

00:29:48.314 --> 00:29:50.475
The Doctor has informed us that

00:29:50.517 --> 00:29:51.848
there is no other
plausible explanation

00:29:51.885 --> 00:29:53.182
for the medical anomalies,
Commander.

00:29:53.219 --> 00:29:55.710
If you don't mind, I'd like
to hear her explanation before

00:29:55.755 --> 00:29:56.779
we dismiss it.

00:29:56.823 --> 00:29:59.121
- Has she been told?
- No.

00:29:59.159 --> 00:30:00.717
I'd like to be the one
who questions her.

00:30:00.760 --> 00:30:04.127
I suggest we wait
until we retrieve the console.

00:30:04.164 --> 00:30:05.654
Janeway to Torres.

00:30:05.698 --> 00:30:06.665
Yes, Captain.

00:30:06.699 --> 00:30:07.961
Your status.

00:30:08.034 --> 00:30:10.730
We are finished
with the computer simulations.

00:30:10.770 --> 00:30:12.965
Everything looks okay.
We're ready to beam over.

00:30:13.039 --> 00:30:15.872
Good. Then let's get started.
Janeway out.

00:30:15.909 --> 00:30:19.106
You were working for her;
Seska was working for them.

00:30:19.145 --> 00:30:21.875
Was anyone on board
that ship working for me?

00:30:21.915 --> 00:30:23.940
The Kazon ship is hailing us.

00:30:23.983 --> 00:30:25.473
Open a channel.

00:30:26.986 --> 00:30:28.954
On screen.

00:30:28.988 --> 00:30:32.583
Our sensors show that you are
trespassing on our vessel.

00:30:32.625 --> 00:30:35.287
As I've already informed you,
we're attempting

00:30:35.328 --> 00:30:38.297
to retrieve the console
that caused this explosion.

00:30:38.331 --> 00:30:41.994
If you attempt to remove
anything from our ship,

00:30:42.102 --> 00:30:44.366
it will be considered
an act of war.

00:30:44.404 --> 00:30:47.396
You know, I'm really easy
to get along with

00:30:47.440 --> 00:30:49.408
most of the time...

00:30:49.442 --> 00:30:52.605
but I don't like bullies,
and I don't like threats,

00:30:52.645 --> 00:30:55.944
and I don't like you, Culluh.

00:31:00.286 --> 00:31:03.380
You can try and stop us
from getting to the truth,

00:31:03.423 --> 00:31:05.618
but I promise you, if you do,

00:31:05.658 --> 00:31:08.786
I will respond with
all the "unique" technologies

00:31:08.828 --> 00:31:10.295
at my command.

00:31:10.330 --> 00:31:12.195
Janeway out.

00:31:12.232 --> 00:31:14.530
Their weapons systems
are standing down.

00:31:14.567 --> 00:31:17.695
They do not appear to be posing
a threat to us at this time.

00:31:17.737 --> 00:31:19.967
At least not until
reinforcements get here.

00:31:20.006 --> 00:31:21.064
Janeway to away team.

00:31:21.107 --> 00:31:22.233
Yes, Captain?

00:31:22.275 --> 00:31:23.936
I don't want to rush you,
Lieutenant, but...

00:31:23.977 --> 00:31:25.444
We're finished, Captain.

00:31:25.478 --> 00:31:26.945
I beg your pardon?

00:31:26.980 --> 00:31:29.278
Decontamination
went exactly as planned.

00:31:29.315 --> 00:31:32.148
The console has been transported
to Engineering,

00:31:32.185 --> 00:31:33.675
and we're on our way back now.

00:31:33.720 --> 00:31:34.778
Acknowledged.

00:31:34.821 --> 00:31:36.345
Well done, away team.

00:31:36.389 --> 00:31:38.254
We'll meet you in Engineering.

00:31:50.436 --> 00:31:53.735
Of all the things to die for.

00:31:55.441 --> 00:31:57.807
It's a food replicator...

00:31:57.844 --> 00:32:01.075
or at least it was trying to be.

00:32:01.114 --> 00:32:03.605
We may take replicators
for granted,

00:32:03.650 --> 00:32:05.709
but imagine what it would mean

00:32:05.752 --> 00:32:08.812
to a culture that doesn't have
this technology.

00:32:08.855 --> 00:32:11.949
They didn't use a thick enough
interior shield casing.

00:32:12.025 --> 00:32:14.459
Once the nucleonic radiation
leaked out,

00:32:14.494 --> 00:32:16.655
a cascade reaction
was inevitable.

00:32:16.696 --> 00:32:19.824
Can you tell if any part of
the console came from our ship?

00:32:19.866 --> 00:32:21.561
There's no doubt about it,
Captain.

00:32:21.601 --> 00:32:23.262
The pattern buffer relays

00:32:23.303 --> 00:32:25.828
are clearly composed
of bio-neural fibers.

00:32:25.872 --> 00:32:28.363
No other Federation ship
would have them.

00:32:28.408 --> 00:32:33.573
Somebody on board Voyager
gave them what they needed.

00:32:33.613 --> 00:32:36.446
I guess they just didn't know
what to do with it.

00:32:36.482 --> 00:32:39.508
I want a complete report
on everything we've found,

00:32:39.552 --> 00:32:42.988
so I can share it
with our Kazon friends.

00:32:57.270 --> 00:33:00.103
We've recovered the console.

00:33:00.139 --> 00:33:02.073
It's a replicator,

00:33:02.108 --> 00:33:06.067
constructed with materials
from Voyager.

00:33:06.112 --> 00:33:07.773
I suppose now everyone thinks

00:33:07.814 --> 00:33:10.408
I went over there
to destroy the evidence.

00:33:12.452 --> 00:33:13.749
Did you?

00:33:13.786 --> 00:33:18.951
I was only trying to show
everyone... show you...

00:33:20.793 --> 00:33:25.423
You really think I had something
to do with this, don't you?

00:33:25.465 --> 00:33:29.799
To be honest,
I'm not sure anymore.

00:33:29.836 --> 00:33:32.304
I'm not sure of a lot of things.

00:33:32.338 --> 00:33:34.431
Then why don't you go talk
to your animal guide

00:33:34.474 --> 00:33:36.101
and figure it all out?

00:33:36.142 --> 00:33:37.609
I plan to.

00:33:37.644 --> 00:33:39.111
Good.

00:33:39.145 --> 00:33:41.477
Get back to me when you do.

00:33:43.549 --> 00:33:45.676
You know, it's funny...

00:33:45.718 --> 00:33:47.709
I've been thinking
about what's been real

00:33:47.754 --> 00:33:49.016
and what's not been real.

00:33:51.257 --> 00:33:53.316
What is this about?

00:33:53.359 --> 00:33:56.487
What's wrong with you?

00:33:56.529 --> 00:33:57.996
Talk to me, Chakotay.

00:33:58.064 --> 00:34:00.089
You owe me that much.

00:34:03.770 --> 00:34:05.237
What would you say

00:34:05.271 --> 00:34:08.104
I owed to a Cardassian
who infiltrated my crew?

00:34:08.141 --> 00:34:11.042
What are you talking about?

00:34:11.077 --> 00:34:12.635
Isn't that why you
never got around

00:34:12.679 --> 00:34:14.613
to a blood analysis
when we came on board?

00:34:14.647 --> 00:34:16.137
I didn't get around to it

00:34:16.182 --> 00:34:17.945
because I didn't
get around to it.

00:34:18.017 --> 00:34:19.075
Turns out your blood is missing

00:34:19.118 --> 00:34:20.415
all the common
Bajoran blood factors.

00:34:20.453 --> 00:34:23.854
It's a side effect
of Orkett's disease.

00:34:23.890 --> 00:34:25.187
Ask your doctor.

00:34:25.224 --> 00:34:27.158
Orkett's disease?

00:34:27.193 --> 00:34:30.128
A childhood virus that swept
through the Bajoran work camps

00:34:30.163 --> 00:34:31.824
during the Occupation.

00:34:31.864 --> 00:34:33.923
Thousands of children
didn't survive.

00:34:33.966 --> 00:34:37.094
I did, thanks
to a bone marrow transplant

00:34:37.136 --> 00:34:39.627
from a sympathetic
Cardassian woman.

00:34:39.672 --> 00:34:41.139
Her name was Kattell.

00:34:41.174 --> 00:34:45.406
When we get home,
you can ask her yourself.

00:34:48.314 --> 00:34:52.375
You must think I'm horrible.

00:34:52.418 --> 00:34:55.546
Do you think I gave you my...

00:34:55.588 --> 00:34:59.991
my heart to get
your Maquis secrets?

00:35:00.093 --> 00:35:03.688
I was starting to wonder.

00:35:05.765 --> 00:35:08.893
Let me tell you something...

00:35:08.935 --> 00:35:12.393
your secrets
weren't good enough.

00:35:12.438 --> 00:35:14.770
They wouldn't have been worth
the trouble

00:35:14.807 --> 00:35:16.741
for a Cardassian agent.

00:35:16.776 --> 00:35:20.576
I had only one agenda
with you, Chakotay,

00:35:20.613 --> 00:35:23.081
and I never kept it secret.

00:35:26.452 --> 00:35:29.888
So, you believe in me again?

00:35:32.625 --> 00:35:34.456
I want to.

00:35:34.494 --> 00:35:38.260
Good, because I want
to go back to work.

00:35:38.297 --> 00:35:39.924
Let's not rush things.

00:35:39.966 --> 00:35:42.093
No, I'm going stir-crazy
in here.

00:35:42.135 --> 00:35:44.103
You're going to have
to stay confined,

00:35:44.137 --> 00:35:45.468
at least until we find out

00:35:45.505 --> 00:35:48.633
exactly where the replicator
components were taken from.

00:35:48.674 --> 00:35:50.938
Well, what'll that tell you?

00:35:50.977 --> 00:35:52.877
There might be evidence
of who took them.

00:35:52.912 --> 00:35:54.971
Oh, you don't think
whoever did this

00:35:55.014 --> 00:35:58.643
is foolish enough to log in
using their own name?

00:35:59.952 --> 00:36:03.012
Chief Inspector Tuvok
leaves no stone unturned.

00:36:05.691 --> 00:36:07.818
I'll tell the Captain
what you told me.

00:36:07.860 --> 00:36:10.886
Somehow, we'll try
to clear this up soon.

00:36:24.110 --> 00:36:27.409
She said a Cardassian
bone marrow transplant

00:36:27.447 --> 00:36:29.745
saved her life as a child.

00:36:29.782 --> 00:36:33.411
Did you set our plan in motion?

00:36:33.453 --> 00:36:36.752
I gave Lieutenant Carey
the same information.

00:36:36.789 --> 00:36:41.624
Now all we can do is wait
and hope someone takes the bait.

00:37:06.886 --> 00:37:09.184
Gin.

00:37:09.222 --> 00:37:13.181
I never knew Vulcans
had such a talent for cards.

00:37:13.226 --> 00:37:15.251
It is simply a matter
of logical discards,

00:37:15.294 --> 00:37:17.922
which give a false impression
of my own requirements

00:37:18.030 --> 00:37:20.123
and deny the needed cards
to your hand.

00:37:20.166 --> 00:37:21.861
I believe that's
94 points to me.

00:37:21.901 --> 00:37:23.892
If you ever need a sponsor
in a gin tournament,

00:37:23.936 --> 00:37:25.369
let me know.

00:37:25.404 --> 00:37:27.668
We're picking up
two more Kazon warships,

00:37:27.707 --> 00:37:29.038
about six hours away.

00:37:29.075 --> 00:37:30.872
We're not going to be able
to stay here much...

00:37:32.411 --> 00:37:35.209
That sounds like a nibble to me.

00:37:39.852 --> 00:37:41.877
Someone is accessing
the inventory database.

00:37:41.921 --> 00:37:43.154
And they're going straight

00:37:43.287 --> 00:37:44.219
to the missing
replicator materials.

00:37:44.255 --> 00:37:46.280
Should we start the trace now?

00:37:46.323 --> 00:37:47.415
Negative.
It might alert them.

00:37:47.458 --> 00:37:48.516
They're entering data.

00:37:48.559 --> 00:37:50.049
Intriguing.
It appears as though

00:37:50.094 --> 00:37:51.618
they're trying to place evidence

00:37:51.662 --> 00:37:54.529
at the scene of the crime
to indicate the guilty party.

00:37:54.565 --> 00:37:57.159
They're entering
an encrypted security code

00:37:57.201 --> 00:37:59.192
into the materials
requisition file.

00:37:59.236 --> 00:38:01.534
Which would suggest
they're hiding it,

00:38:01.572 --> 00:38:03.199
but not very well.

00:38:03.240 --> 00:38:06.869
Anybody know whose security code
that belongs to?

00:38:06.911 --> 00:38:09.038
I do.

00:38:09.079 --> 00:38:11.570
It's Seska's.

00:38:13.751 --> 00:38:16.720
Then it has to be Carey.

00:38:16.754 --> 00:38:20.918
Carey is trying to point
the finger at Seska.

00:38:37.975 --> 00:38:40.910
Chakotay...

00:38:40.945 --> 00:38:43.243
is anything wrong?

00:38:43.280 --> 00:38:44.907
It's over.

00:38:44.949 --> 00:38:48.112
We know who gave the technology
to the Kazon.

00:38:51.188 --> 00:38:52.655
Who?

00:38:52.690 --> 00:38:54.783
You did.

00:38:56.660 --> 00:39:00.187
Look, I don't know what evidence
you think you've found, but...

00:39:00.231 --> 00:39:01.721
We found the evidence

00:39:01.765 --> 00:39:03.824
you put there for us to find...

00:39:03.867 --> 00:39:05.767
your own security code.

00:39:05.803 --> 00:39:08.897
I have no idea
what you're talking about.

00:39:08.973 --> 00:39:12.306
We already knew where the stolen
materials had been taken from

00:39:12.343 --> 00:39:14.368
before I met with you.

00:39:14.411 --> 00:39:16.675
We were monitoring
the inventory manifest,

00:39:16.714 --> 00:39:19.911
hoping either you or Carey
would try to cover your tracks.

00:39:19.984 --> 00:39:22.282
Hell of a way for me
to cover my tracks...

00:39:22.319 --> 00:39:25.049
putting in my own security code
for you to find?

00:39:25.089 --> 00:39:26.579
That's exactly what you did.

00:39:26.624 --> 00:39:29.650
You knew no one would believe
you could be that careless.

00:39:29.693 --> 00:39:30.921
You wanted us to believe

00:39:31.028 --> 00:39:33.258
that someone else
was trying to frame you.

00:39:33.297 --> 00:39:35.788
Ever consider
that maybe someone was?

00:39:35.833 --> 00:39:39.325
We traced the computer station
used to enter the data.

00:39:39.370 --> 00:39:42.737
Oh, you took us all around
the system and back again

00:39:42.773 --> 00:39:45.105
before we could locate
the source,

00:39:45.142 --> 00:39:49.135
but it was this station
in Sick Bay.

00:39:52.283 --> 00:39:55.309
I'd almost say
it was a Maquis operation,

00:39:55.352 --> 00:39:58.583
if I didn't already know
you were a Cardassian.

00:39:58.622 --> 00:40:03.389
Computer, activate Emergency
Holographic Medical Program.

00:40:04.461 --> 00:40:06.088
Ah.

00:40:06.130 --> 00:40:10.089
Have I been called to testify?

00:40:10.134 --> 00:40:13.297
Before you even mentioned
Orkett's disease to me,

00:40:13.337 --> 00:40:16.135
the doctor had
already discounted that

00:40:16.173 --> 00:40:18.300
as a possible explanation
for your blood anomalies.

00:40:18.342 --> 00:40:19.536
And may I say

00:40:19.576 --> 00:40:21.305
a doctor less informed
about Bajoran medicine

00:40:21.345 --> 00:40:23.939
might have been fooled,
but my program includes

00:40:23.981 --> 00:40:26.916
the complete Bajoran medical
text on Orkett's disease.

00:40:26.950 --> 00:40:28.884
There's no way
any childhood virus

00:40:28.919 --> 00:40:30.978
or Cardassian
bone marrow transplant

00:40:31.021 --> 00:40:33.251
can explain away the genetic
markers in your blood.

00:40:33.290 --> 00:40:34.882
You are Cardassian, Ensign.

00:40:34.925 --> 00:40:37.655
But that didn't necessarily
make you the traitor

00:40:37.695 --> 00:40:39.663
we were looking for.

00:40:39.697 --> 00:40:43.793
We needed more evidence,
and you gave it to us.

00:40:43.834 --> 00:40:47.998
The one thing
I still can't understand is...

00:40:48.105 --> 00:40:49.663
why?

00:40:51.275 --> 00:40:54.005
I did it for you.

00:40:54.044 --> 00:40:58.003
I did it for this crew.

00:40:58.048 --> 00:40:59.948
We are alone here,

00:40:59.983 --> 00:41:02.952
at the mercy
of any number of hostile aliens

00:41:02.986 --> 00:41:05.784
because of
the incomprehensible decision

00:41:05.823 --> 00:41:08.417
of a Federation Captain.

00:41:08.459 --> 00:41:11.326
A Federation Captain
who destroyed

00:41:11.362 --> 00:41:13.592
our only chance to get home.

00:41:13.630 --> 00:41:16.428
Federation rules,

00:41:16.467 --> 00:41:19.095
Federation nobility,

00:41:19.136 --> 00:41:21.263
Federation compassion?

00:41:21.305 --> 00:41:22.602
Do you understand?

00:41:22.639 --> 00:41:26.131
If this had been a Cardassian
ship, we would be home now.

00:41:26.176 --> 00:41:29.202
We must begin
to forge alliances.

00:41:29.246 --> 00:41:31.976
To survive,
we must have powerful friends.

00:41:32.049 --> 00:41:35.485
The Kazon-Nistrim were willing
to be our protectors

00:41:35.519 --> 00:41:37.919
in return
for some minor technology.

00:41:37.955 --> 00:41:40.150
Minor technology
that could change

00:41:40.190 --> 00:41:42.681
the balance of power
in this Quadrant.

00:41:42.726 --> 00:41:43.886
Change it in our favor.

00:41:43.927 --> 00:41:46.361
That is all that matters
at this point...

00:41:46.397 --> 00:41:49.059
building a base of power
in this Quadrant.

00:41:51.335 --> 00:41:54.827
You are a fool, Captain.

00:41:54.872 --> 00:41:57.602
And you're a fool to follow her.

00:41:57.641 --> 00:42:01.907
I can't imagine
how I ever loved you.

00:42:03.647 --> 00:42:04.944
Computer, Command XJL.

00:42:04.982 --> 00:42:08.418
Computer,
override transport in progress.

00:42:08.452 --> 00:42:11.478
Unable to comply.
Security lockout is in place.

00:42:11.522 --> 00:42:14.753
Computer, identify destination
of transport.

00:42:14.792 --> 00:42:18.159
A Kazon vessel,
14 kilometers off the port bow.

00:42:18.195 --> 00:42:19.253
Bridge to Janeway.

00:42:19.296 --> 00:42:20.786
- Go ahead.
- The Kazon ship

00:42:20.831 --> 00:42:21.889
is powering up its engines.

00:42:21.932 --> 00:42:23.695
It looks like they're
getting ready to go to warp.

00:42:23.734 --> 00:42:25.065
Ready a tractor beam.

00:42:25.102 --> 00:42:26.763
I've also got two Kazon warships

00:42:26.804 --> 00:42:29.432
on an intercept course
less than ten minutes away.

00:42:29.473 --> 00:42:32.806
Captain, even with our superior
defense capabilities,

00:42:32.843 --> 00:42:36.142
we cannot prevail against
three Kazon warships.

00:42:36.180 --> 00:42:39.445
Awaiting your instructions,
Captain.

00:42:39.483 --> 00:42:41.644
Power down the tractor beam.

00:42:41.685 --> 00:42:44.882
Set a course out of here,
Mr. Paris, warp four.

00:42:44.922 --> 00:42:46.446
Engage when ready.

00:42:46.490 --> 00:42:47.980
Yes, ma'am.

00:42:48.091 --> 00:42:52.152
We'll have to wait for another
day to settle up with Seska.

00:43:08.445 --> 00:43:11.209
Can I ask you to be honest
with me, Lieutenant?

00:43:11.248 --> 00:43:14.149
As a Vulcan, I am at all
times honest, Commander.

00:43:15.452 --> 00:43:17.443
That's not exactly true.

00:43:17.488 --> 00:43:18.785
You lied to me

00:43:18.822 --> 00:43:20.949
when you passed yourself off
as a Maquis to get on my crew.

00:43:20.991 --> 00:43:22.583
I was honest
to my own convictions

00:43:22.626 --> 00:43:24.719
within the defined
parameters of my mission.

00:43:24.761 --> 00:43:27.958
You damned Vulcans
and your defined parameters.

00:43:27.998 --> 00:43:29.625
That's easy for you.

00:43:29.666 --> 00:43:32.134
On the contrary, the demands
on a Vulcan's character

00:43:32.169 --> 00:43:34.296
are extraordinarily difficult.

00:43:34.338 --> 00:43:38.468
Do not mistake composure
for ease.

00:43:38.509 --> 00:43:41.273
How may I be honest
with you today?

00:43:47.918 --> 00:43:49.749
I'd just like to know...

00:43:49.786 --> 00:43:54.655
from someone else who pulled
the wool over my eyes...

00:43:54.691 --> 00:43:57.159
was I particularly naive?

00:43:57.194 --> 00:43:58.661
Was I not paying
enough attention?

00:43:58.695 --> 00:44:01.095
What the hell was it that let
all you spies get by me?

00:44:01.131 --> 00:44:03.429
Like all humans,

00:44:03.467 --> 00:44:06.197
you depend on feelings
and instincts to guide you,

00:44:06.236 --> 00:44:09.069
and they invariably
let you down.

00:44:09.106 --> 00:44:10.073
But "particularly naive"?

00:44:10.107 --> 00:44:13.235
No, Commander,
and I've always considered

00:44:13.277 --> 00:44:15.507
your attention span
to be adequate.

00:44:15.546 --> 00:44:17.707
Did you ever see anything
about Seska

00:44:17.748 --> 00:44:19.545
that made you suspicious?

00:44:19.583 --> 00:44:21.050
No.

00:44:21.084 --> 00:44:22.517
She quite expertly

00:44:22.553 --> 00:44:24.953
"pulled the wool" over my eyes,
as well.

00:44:24.988 --> 00:44:26.615
Well...

00:44:26.657 --> 00:44:30.252
that makes me feel
a little better.

00:44:30.294 --> 00:44:31.591
Thanks.

00:44:31.628 --> 00:44:32.925
Curious.

00:44:32.963 --> 00:44:34.362
What?

00:44:34.398 --> 00:44:36.332
That my failure,
added to your own,

00:44:36.366 --> 00:44:38.061
should improve your feelings.

00:44:40.470 --> 00:44:43.132
Misery loves company, Tuvok.
